   229	
   230	# Verify Acceptance Release
   231	
   232	## Goal
   233	
   234	Decide what the evidence actually proves without sharing the implementation role's authority or silently repairing the definition of done. Operate read-only by default.
   235	
   236	## Independence Boundary
   237	
   238	- Use a different session, context, or authorized human reviewer from the implementation role whenever practical.
   239	- Review the original request, every decision-scoped acceptance fragment in the requested release scope, its decision semantic key, accepted version, and invalidation keys, task-local `acceptance/index.md`, project-level `acceptance/index.md`, declared human `binding.md` and `checklist.md`, approval evidence, protected-test hashes, implementation diff identity, and raw test/runtime evidence.
   240	- Do not edit implementation or tests during review. If the user explicitly requests fixes, return findings to `$implement-acceptance-locked-change`, then rereview only the changed findings and affected evidence.
   241	- Reuse a prior review when contract, source diff, protected-test hashes, environment identity, and evidence identity are unchanged.
   242	
   243	## Decision-Scoped Verification And Local Reuse
   244	
   245	When an SSOT governs the change, validate the `.ssot` machine source and select review work from explicit decision, acceptance, implementation, evidence, and resource edges. Do not wait for an entire SSOT stage before reviewing a completed decision-scoped acceptance fragment. Fragment-level review may establish reusable evidence and findings, but it cannot declare the whole release `READY`.
   246	
   247	Bind every review lane to the fragment hash, decision semantic key, accepted version, and invalidation keys it evaluates. When an upstream decision or contract changes, reverify only evidence lanes whose invalidation keys match and any downstream synthesis that consumed them. Do not rerun every evidence lane or discard unrelated signed human results. Unchanged decision refs and evidence identities remain reusable.
   248	
   249	After all blocking fragments and shared convergence outputs in the declared release scope are accepted, one release-review owner makes one final serial release decision. Global completeness belongs only at that final synthesis boundary; it must not block earlier fragment review.
   250	
   251	## Maximum-Safe Parallel Verification
   252	
   253	Pin the selected fragment versions/hashes, decision refs, protected-test baselines, source diff, runtime identity, evidence identities, required roles, and one release-review owner serially. Then inventory all independent review surfaces and calculate:
   254	
   255	```text
   256	LOGICAL_LANE_TARGET = READY_INDEPENDENT_DELIVERABLES
   257	ACTUAL_CONCURRENCY = min(LOGICAL_LANE_TARGET, AVAILABLE_WRITABLE_L2_SLOTS)
   258	WAVE_COUNT = ceil(LOGICAL_LANE_TARGET / AVAILABLE_WRITABLE_L2_SLOTS)
   259	```
